{% extends "synthesis_layout.jinja2" %}

{% block category_task %}
Write an authoritative encyclopedia article on the community: **{{ topic_name }}**.
{% endblock %}

{% block category_architecture %}
1. THE ORIENTING LEDE (NO SUBHEADING):
   - 1 concise paragraph defining the community, geographic distribution, language family, and economic or cultural footprint.
2. SOCIAL & CULTURAL BODY:
   - Organize into 2 to 4 '{{ body_heading_prefix }}' subheadings (e.g., `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Geographic Distribution & Settlement Patterns`, `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Material Culture & Economic Livelihoods`, `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Customary Law & Leadership`).
   {% if subtopics %}
   - Key facets to address: {{ subtopics | join(", ") }}.
   {% endif %}
   - Contextualize historical terminology without endorsing colonial tropes.
3. ETHNOGRAPHIC & LINGUISTIC RECORD:
   - Conclude with `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Research and Documentation` surveying recorded folklore, wordlists, and early anthropological accounts in the literature.
{% endblock %}